  }\n\n    .methodology,\n    .results {\n      width: 100%;\n    }\n\n    .method-body {\n      padding: 30px 22px 0;\n    }\n\n    .subheading {\n      margin: 0;\n      font-size: 24px;\n      line-height: 29px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n    }\n\n    .method-section {\n      margin: 0 0 37px;\n    }\n\n    .method-section p,\n    .result-section p {\n      margin: 11px 0 0;\n      font-size: 25px;\n      line-height: 34px;\n    }\n\n    .method-section:nth-child(2) {\n      margin-bottom: 38px;\n    }\n\n    .method-section:nth-child(3) {\n      margin-bottom: 38px;\n    }\n\n    .method-section:nth-child(4) {\n      margin-bottom: 37px;\n    }\n\n    .results-body {\n      padding: 18px 26px 0;\n    }\n\n    .optimal-section p {\n      margin-top: 13px;\n    }\n\n    .temperature-section {\n      margin-top: 39px;\n    }\n\n    .temperature-list {\n      margin: 14px 0 0;\n      padding-left: 25px;\n      font-size: 25px;\n      line-height: 34px;\n      list-style-type: square;\n    }\n\n    .temperature-list li {\n      padding-left: 0;\n      margin: 0 0 7px;\n    }\n\n    .table-section {\n      margin-top: 47px;\n    }\n\n    .table-section .subheading {\n      margin-bottom: 18px;\n    }\n\n    .data-table-wrap {\n      width: 573px;\n      height: 349px;\n      margin-left: -26px;\n      padding: 25px 40px 18px;\n      background: linear-gradient(105deg, #91d8e7 0%, #cef2e8 100%);\n    }\n\n    table {\n      width: 100%;\n      height: 100%;\n      border-collapse: collapse;\n      table-layout: fixed;\n      font-size: 20px;\n      line-height: 25px;\n    }\n\n    th {\n      height: 47px;\n      text-align: left;\n      font-size: 20px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,.65);\n    }\n\n    td {\n      height: 55px;\n      text-align: left;\n      border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,.58);\n    }\n\n    th:first-child,\n    td:first-child {\n      width: 50%;\n    }\n\n    .footer-note {\n      width: 1243px;\n      height: 75px;\n      border-top: 2px solid #555555;\n      padding: 20px 0 0 82px;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      line-height: 24px;\n    }\n\n    .sidebar {\n      width: 485px;\n      min-height: 1938px;\n      padding: 29px 47px 40px 32px;\n      background: linear-gradient(110deg, #88d3e4 0%, #c6f2e7 100%);\n    }\n\n    .side-block {\n      width: 406px;\n      margin: 0;\n    }\n\n    .side-block + .side-block {\n      margin-top: 22px;\n    }\n\n    .side-heading {\n      width: 406px;\n      height: 76px;\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 0 22px;\n      display: flex;\n      align-items: center;\n      background: #ffffff;\n      font-size: 38px;\n      line-height: 1;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      white-space: nowrap;\n    }\n\n    .side-copy {\n      margin: 10px 10px 0;\n      font-size: 25px;\n      line-height: 34px;\n    }\n\n    .references .side-copy {\n      margin-top: 12px;\n      margin-left: 10px;\n      margin-right: 0;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      line-height: 22px;\n    }\n\n    .reference-item {\n      margin: 0 0 20px;\n      padding-left: 14px;\n      position: relative;\n    }\n\n    .reference-item::before {\n      content: \"▪\";\n      position: absolute;\n      left: 0;\n      top: 0;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <header class=\"title-band\">\n    <h1>\n      EXPLORING THE EFFECT OF TEMPERATURE<br>\n      ON ENZYME ACTIVITY IN PLANT CELLS\n    </h1>\n  </header>\n\n  <nav class=\"names-area\" aria-label=\"Contributors\">\n    <div class=\"names-strip\">\n      <div>• Alex G.</div>\n      <div>• Monica V.</div>\n      <div>• Tessa H.</div>\n      <div>• Aiko S.</div>\n      <div>• Bill T.</div>\n    </div>\n  </nav>\n\n  <main class=\"page-layout\">\n    <div class=\"left-page\">\n      <div class=\"top-row\">\n        <section class=\"introduction\">\n          <h2 class=\"section-heading\">INTRODUCTION</h2>\n          <p class=\"intro-copy\">\n            Enzymes are essential biological catalysts<br>\n            that regulate chemical reactions within<br>\n            cells. This study investigates how<br>\n            temperature influences enzyme activity in<br>\n            plant cells, specifically focusing on<br>\n            amylase, an enzyme that catalyzes the<br>\n            breakdown of starch. Understanding the<br>\n            relationship between temperature and<br>\n            enzyme activity can help optimize<br>\n            agricultural practices, such as enhancing<br>\n            crop resistance to temperature<br>\n            fluctuations and improving the efficiency<br>\n            of industrial processes that involve plant-<br>\n            based enzymes.\n          </p>\n        </section>\n\n        <figure class=\"placeholder photo-placeholder\" aria-label=\"[Photo: succulent plant]\">\n          <figcaption class=\"caption\">[Photo: succulent plant]</figcaption>\n        </figure>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"lower-row\">\n        <section class=\"methodology\">\n          <h2 class=\"section-heading\">METHODOLOGY</h2>\n          <div class=\"method-body\">\n            <div class=\"method-section\">\n              <h3 class=\"subheading\">SAMPLE PREPARATION</h3>\n              <p>\n                Corn leaf cells were isolated and<br>\n                homogenized to extract amylase<br>\n                enzymes. The enzyme activity was<br>\n                measured by the rate of starch<br>\n                breakdown.\n              </p>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"method-section\">\n              <h3 class=\"subheading\">TEMPERATURE VARIATION</h3>\n              <p>\n                Enzyme activity was tested at 0°C,<br>\n                20°C, 40°C, 60°C, and 80°C.<br>\n                Reactions were incubated for 30<br>\n                minutes at each temperature.\n              </p>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"method-section\">\n              <h3 class=\"subheading\">SUBSTRATE ADDITION</h3>\n              <p>\n                Starch solution was added to each<br>\n                reaction, providing a substrate for<br>\n                the amylase enzyme.\n              </p>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"method-section\">\n              <h3 class=\"subheading\">REACTION TERMINATION</h3>\n              <p>\n                The reactions were stopped after 30<br>\n                minutes using an enzyme inhibitor,<br>\n                and glucose production was<br>\n                measured.\n              </p>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"method-section\">\n              <h3 class=\"subheading\">DATA ANALYSIS</h3>\n              <p>\n                Absorbance of glucose was<br>\n                measured using a<br>\n                spectrophotometer. Data were<br>\n                analyzed using ANOVA to assess<br>\n                statistical significance of<br>\n                temperature on enzyme activity.\n              </p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"results\">\n          <h2 class=\"section-heading\">RESULTS</h2>\n          <div class=\"results-body\">\n            <div class=\"result-section optimal-section\">\n              <h3 class=\"subheading\">OPTIMAL TEMPERATURE</h3>\n              <p>\n                Enzyme activity peaked at 40°C, where the<br>\n                amylase was most effective in catalyzing starch<br>\n                breakdown. At this temperature, the rate of<br>\n                glucose production was 50% higher than at<br>\n                lower or higher temperatures.\n              </p>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"result-section temperature-section\">\n              <h3 class=\"subheading\">TEMPERATURE EFFECT</h3>\n              <ul class=\"temperature-list\">\n                <li>At 0°C, enzyme activity was minimal, with<br>only 10% of the maximum activity observed<br>at 40°C</li>\n                <li>At 20°C, enzyme activity was moderate, with<br>a 30% increase in glucose production<br>compared to 0°C</li>\n                <li>At 60°C, enzyme activity dropped<br>significantly, with only 25% of the activity<br>seen at 40°C</li>\n                <li>At 80°C, enzyme activity was nearly zero,<br>indicating enzyme denaturation</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"result-section table-section\">\n              <h3 class=\"subheading\">TEMPERATURE EFFECT</h3>\n              <div class=\"data-table-wrap\">\n                <table>\n                  <thead>\n                    <tr>\n                      <th>TEMPERATURE (°C)</th>\n                      <th>ENZYME ACTIVITY</th>\n                    </tr>\n                  </thead>\n                  <tbody>\n                    <tr>\n                      <td>0</td>\n                      <td>0.1</td>\n                    </tr>\n                    <tr>\n                      <td>20</td>\n                      <td>0.3</td>\n                    </tr>\n                    <tr>\n                      <td>40</td>\n                      <td>0.5</td>\n                    </tr>\n                    <tr>\n                      <td>60</td>\n                      <td>0.25</td>\n                    </tr>\n                    <tr>\n                      <td>80</td>\n                      <td>0.05</td>\n                    </tr>\n                  </tbody>\n                </table>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n      </div>\n\n      <footer class=\"footer-note\">\n        [All information here is for demonstration purposes and does not reflect actual data or outcomes.]\n      </footer>\n    </div>\n\n    <aside class=\"sidebar\">\n      <section class=\"side-block discussion\">\n        <h2 class=\"side-heading\">DISCUSSION</h2>\n        <p class=\"side-copy\">\n          The results suggest that<br>\n          temperature has a profound<br>\n          impact on enzyme activity, with<br>\n          amylase being most efficient at<br>\n          40°C. The significant decline in<br>\n          activity at temperatures above<br>\n          60°C supports the hypothesis that<br>\n          extreme heat denatures enzymes.<br>\n          This has implications for both<br>\n          agricultural biotechnology, where<br>\n          temperature resilience could be<br>\n          engineered, and for industrial<br>\n          enzyme applications, where<br>\n          optimal reaction conditions are<br>\n          critical for efficiency.\n        </p>\n      </section>\n\n      <section class=\"side-block conclusion\">\n        <h2 class=\"side-heading\">CONCLUSION</h2>\n        <p class=\"side-copy\">\n          Amylase activity in plant cells is<br>\n          highly temperature-dependent,<br>\n          with an optimal temperature of<br>\n          40°C for maximum efficiency.<br>\n          Understanding the temperature<br>\n          sensitivity of enzymes can help<br>\n          improve crop productivity under<br>\n          varying environmental conditions<br>\n          and optimize industrial enzyme<br>\n          processes.\n        </p>\n      </section>\n\n      <section class=\"side-block acknowledgments\">\n        <h2 class=\"side-heading\">ACKNOWLEDGMENTS</h2>\n        <p class=\"side-copy\">\n          This study was funded by the<br>\n          Agricultural Science Research<br>\n          Fund. Special thanks to the Plant<br>\n          Biology Department at Greenfield<br>\n          University for providing the<br>\n          samples.\n        </p>\n      </section>\n\n      <section class=\"side-block references\">\n        <h2 class=\"side-heading\">REFERENCES</h2>\n        <div class=\"side-copy\">\n          <div class=\"reference-item\">\n            Green, J. H., &amp; Thomas, L. M. (2021). Temperature-<br>\n            dependent enzyme activity in plant cells: A<br>\n            comparative study. Journal of Plant Physiology,<br>\n            98(2), 115–130.<br>\n            https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jplphys.2021.0207\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"reference-item\">\n            Zhang, Q., &amp; Chen, Y. F. (2020). Effects of<br>\n            temperature fluctuations on enzyme kinetics in<br>\n            plant systems. Biochemical and Biophysical<br>\n            Research Communications, 53(9), 245–259.<br>\n            https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbrc.2020.0806\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"reference-item\">\n            Patel, S. K., &amp; Rivera, J. A. (2022). The impact of<br>\n            thermal stress on plant enzyme activity: Insights<br>\n            from cellular experiments. Plant Biochemistry<br>\n            Journal, 62(4), 410–425.<br>\n            https://doi.org/10.1098/pbj.2022.0404\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n    </aside>\n  </main>\n</body>\n</html>"
